2026-04-06 13:43:23,779[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-chatcmpl-tool-94c02d0ab841f99a] execute_python_code({"code": "import sympy as sp\n\n# Define the symbols\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Given angles\nangle_ABC = 40\nangle_ACB = 100\nangle_ACD = 50\nangle_BCD = 50\nangle_BAD = 70\nangle_CAD = 70\n\n# Calculate angle BFC (using properties of isosceles triangles)\nangle_BFC = (180 - angle_ACB) / 2\n\n# Using the fact that E is the midpoint of CF, and considering the symmetry and properties of the angles,\n# we can deduce that angle FBG is half of angle BFC.\nangle_FBG = angle_BFC / 2\n\n# Substitute the known values\nangle_FBG_value = angle_FBG\nangle_FBG_value", "timeout": 30}) - MainThread
2026-04-06 13:43:23,784[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-chatcmpl-tool-a1c8fae7986f752b] execute_python_code({"code": "def is_p_safe(n, p):\n    # Check if n is p-safe\n    for k in range((n // p) - 1, (n // p) + 2):\n        if abs(n - k * p) <= 2:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef count_safe_numbers(limit, primes):\n    count = 0\n    for n in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if all(is_p_safe(n, p) for p in primes):\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\nlimit = 10000\nprimes = [7, 11, 13]\nsafe_count = count_safe_numbers(limit, primes)\nsafe_count", "timeout": 30}) - MainThread
